meta {
  name: Stripe Billing Webhook (reference only)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/billing
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  stripe-signature: t=1234567890,v1=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
}

body:text {
  {
    "id": "evt_test_xxxxxxxxxx",
    "type": "checkout.session.completed",
    "data": {
      "object": {
        "id": "cs_test_xxxxxxxxxx",
        "customer_email": "shop@example.com",
        "metadata": {
          "retailerId": "clxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
          "planId": "clxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
          "service": "RECOMMENDATION"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  ## POST /api/webhooks/billing  ⚠️ Do NOT call manually

  Stripe webhook endpoint. Receives and verifies signed events from Stripe.
  The `stripe-signature` header is **mandatory** — Stripe signs every request
  with your `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` and this route verifies it before processing.

  ### Handled Events
  | Event                         | Action                                              |
  |-------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------|
  | `checkout.session.completed`  | Activates subscription in DB                        |
  | `invoice.paid`                | Resets `currentPeriodUsage` to 0 for new period     |
  | `customer.subscription.deleted` | Marks subscription as `EXPIRED`                  |

  > **Testing locally:** Use `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/webhooks/billing`
  > with the Stripe CLI to receive real test events.

  ### Success (200)
  ```json
  { "received": true }
  ```
}
